.TH "PERFORMANCECONTAINERTIMING.PAINTTIME" "3JS" "October 26, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
PerformanceContainerTiming.paintTime \- PerformanceContainerTiming:
paintTime property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]paintTime\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]PerformanceContainerTiming\f[R] interface returns a timestamp that
represents when the rendering phase ended and the paint phase started.
.PP
This property is a broadly interoperable metric for indicating the time
to paint, and can therefore be used when comparing behavior across
browsers.
For single\-browser testing, you can use \f[CR]presentationTime\f[R]
instead.
.SH VALUE
A \f[CR]DOMHighResTimeStamp\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
See Observing how entries change as a container grows in
\f[CR]PerformanceContainerTiming\f[R].
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]PerformanceContainerTiming.presentationTime\f[R]
